---
$ nage user reset-password --help
[stdout]
Give a user a new password and sign them out everywhere

Usage: nage user reset-password [OPTIONS] --by <ADMIN> --username <NAME>

Options:
      --data-dir <DIR>   The data folder that holds nage.sqlite, which must exist and be set up [env: NAGE_DATA_DIR] [default: ./data]
      --by <ADMIN>       The username of the admin who resets the password; it may be the user being reset
      --username <NAME>  The username of the user whose password is reset
      --password-stdin   Read the new password once from standard input instead of asking for it twice at the terminal
  -h, --help             Print help
[stderr]
[exit] 0
